# Another major architectural issue

Right now we have multiple ways to finish a month:

```text
Fixed Draw
    → finishMonth()

Auction
    → directly marks chit_months COMPLETED

Agent Chit
    → finishMonth()

Month Close API
    → separate endpoint
```

That is dangerous for a financial application.

We should have **one authoritative month-close/reconciliation service**.

The ideal lifecycle should be:

```text
COLLECTION
   ↓
all/required payments verified
   ↓
ACTION
   ↓
draw OR auction OR agent-chit
   ↓
payout recorded
   ↓
financial reconciliation
   ↓
ledger entries
   ↓
month close
   ↓
month LOCKED
```

Otherwise it is possible for one path to mark a month completed while another path still thinks it is open.

