* **Agent payment verification was creator-only**, despite the mobile app exposing verification to authorized agents.
* **Payout settlement was creator-only**, conflicting with the multi-agent permission model.
* **Reconciliation was creator-only**, so an assigned Agent could not use it.
* **Month close was creator-only.**
* **AGENT_CHIT settlement was creator-only.**
* **Fixed Draw used `Math.random()`** instead of a stronger server-side random source.
* **Fixed Draw did not consistently return winner name/mobile.**
* **Auction state had no proper “current auction for this month” lookup**, so reopening the mobile screen could lose the auction ID.
* **Auction state authorization was too weak.**
* **Auction winner information wasn't returned in the state response in a mobile-friendly form.**
* **Profile editing was missing from the mobile UI/API.**
* **Reconciliation/month-close screens were missing from mobile.**
* **Agent month still displayed raw JSON in its success alert.**
* Most importantly, **Fixed Draw/Agent Chit were marking months `LOCKED` inside the financial operation before the separate Month Close process**. I changed this architecture so financial completion becomes `COMPLETED`, and the dedicated month-close operation performs the final `LOCKED` transition after payout/obligation checks.

